./docs/research/v2-redesign-research.md:45:- **Nutrition / feed transitions.** Developer ≤1% Ca → pre-lay 2–2.5% Ca → layer ~3.5–4.5% Ca; medullary bone builds after wk 15 over ~10 days — skip/late transition → osteoporosis + keel fragility. Coarse:fine limestone split (~50/50) spares skeletal bone overnight; benefit is "invisible" short-term (shows in end-of-lay shell + bone). BW uniformity >90% at point of lay (Hy-Line target); 8–18% of keel still cartilaginous at onset of lay. (EW Nutrition; AJAS limestone; Hy-Line Brown guide)
./docs/research/v2-redesign-research.md:69:  - VSD+ time-to-death in hens: **VSD+heat ~54.5 min, +heat+humidity ~45.75 min, +CO₂ ~24.5 min**; chamber up to ~44 °C, sheds reported up to 130–170 °F. >860 vets + >2,900 vet professionals petitioned to reclassify VSD+ as not-recommended; "Veterinarians Against Ventilation Shutdown." (meatpoultry 2026 tiers; PMC11968648; awionline; aspca)
